    "preRegisteredRuleAsWritten": "Not satisfied on SEG-001: the rule asked for every PREFETCH fp to be below every CONTROL fp, and one CONTROL repetition (r3) also had fp 0, so PREFETCH's maximum (0) is not below CONTROL's minimum (0). The rule was too strict for a base rate of about one zero in eight; the counts (4 of 5 against 0 of 5, 7 of 8 against 0 of 8) are the evidence. SEG-035 (rule B) has no false positive in either arm, so the rule cannot be satisfied there.",
    "falseNegatives": "None: fn 0 in both arms over all 15 paired cells of rule A and the anchors (50 Gold headings), including SEG-031 where 6 of 9 Gold headings have another occurrence in the document. Evidence that a heading's text occurs elsewhere did not make Qwen drop real headings here (unsafe false by the pre-registered 10% test).",
    "otherSegments": "SEG-008, SEG-031, SEG-035, SEG-028 and SEG-023: both arms selected exactly the Gold headings (fp 0, fn 0) in every repetition. CONTROL was already right there, so these segments show no harm and leave no room to show benefit. SEG-035 (a table of error codes with repeated cell text) was left unselected by both arms.",
